NAME
       echo - display a line of text

SYNOPSIS
       echo [-neE] [STRING]...

DESCRIPTION
       Write the STRINGs separated by spaces, followed by a newline. The shell
       has a built-in echo with the same behavior; /bin/echo is used by
       programs that run it directly.

OPTIONS
       -n
           do not output the trailing newline

       -e
           interpret backslash escapes: \n \t \r \a \b \f \v \e \\ \0NNN \xHH,
           and \c to stop output

       -E
           do not interpret escapes (default)

EXAMPLES
       echo Hello, world
       echo -e 'red: \e[31mtext\e[0m'

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)
